==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|toucher}}, {{m|frm|touchier}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|tochier}}, {{m|fro|touchier}}, {{m|fro|tucher}} (compare French doublet {{doublet|fr|toquer|notext=1}}, from unattested {{inh|fr|VL.||*toccāre|t=to knock, strike, offend}}, from {{der|fr|frk|*tokkōn}}, {{m|frk|*tukkōn|t=to touch}}, from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*tukkōną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*tukkijaną|t=to jerk, knock, strike, offend}}, from {{der|fr|ine-pro|*dewk-|t=to lead, pull, draw}}, influenced by proximity to similar forms from {{cog|gem-pro|*tēkaną|t=to touch}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|zochhōn|t=to grasp, seize}}, {{cog|goh|zuchôn|t=to jerk, tug}}, {{cog|gml|-}} {{m|gmh|tucken|t=to tug}}, {{cog|odt|tocken}}, {{m|odt|tucken|t=to touch, entise}}, {{cog|ang|tucian}}, {{m|ang|tūcian|t=to mistreat, disturb, torment}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐌴𐌺𐌰𐌽|t=to touch}}, {{cog|non|taka|t=to touch grasp}}, {{cog|ang|tacan|t=to touch, take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-toucher.ogg|Audio (France, Paris)}}
* {{rhymes|fr|e}}
* {{homophones|fr|touchai|touché|touchée|touchées|touchers|touchés|touchez}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# The act of [[touching]] {{qualifier|see below}}.
# A way of touching.
# The sense of [[touch]], [[tactility]].

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{lb|fr|transitive}} To [[touch]] (physically).
#: {{uxi|fr|Ne me '''touche''' pas !|Don't touch me!}}
# {{lb|fr|transitive}} To [[affect]]
#: {{uxi|fr|La maladie '''touche''' actuellement 2 millions de personnes.|The disease currently affects 2 million people.}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive|followed by "{{l|fr|à}}"}} To [[try]], to [[try out]].
#: {{uxi|fr|Je n'ai jamais '''touché''' au tabac.|I've never tried tobacco.}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive|colloquial}} Short for [[toucher sa bille]]. To be skillful.
#: {{uxi|fr|Ce mec est un ancien critique d'art. Je peux te dire qu'il '''touche''' en peinture !|This guy is a former art critic. Believe me, he knows a thing or two about painting!}}
# {{lb|fr|transitive|money, income}} to [[receive]], to [[get]]

